            view: "**A real defence business inside a rebuild that has not paid for itself yet.** Defence revenue doubled to ₹125cr in Q1, with sole-source content on BrahMos and Uttam. But the retained business made ₹8.7cr of operating profit against ₹8.9cr of interest and ₹8.8cr of depreciation, group operating profit was ₹27.9cr as reported against ₹41.0cr after management's own adjustments (₹13.1cr of 'one-off' provisions, mostly on an old defence receivable), only about ₹910cr of the ₹2,256cr sale price arrives soon against ₹2,100–2,250cr of plans, its first acquisition (Cloud Wave, ₹234cr) was paid for with 12.5% debt, the promoter sold 10.86% of the company in late September, and guidance has moved to a 'pro forma annualised' basis.",
            watch: 'Both phases of sale proceeds actually received; no repeat of the ₹13.1cr of one-off provisions, and the kept business covering interest and depreciation on reported profit by Q4 FY27; aerospace reaching its ₹375cr yearly run rate by Q4; XiDA growing without counting the business transferred in; Cloud Wave earning more than the 12.5% it pays on the debt that bought it; any further selling by the promoter, Jupiter Capital, after its 10.86% sale in September.',
